+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry owns validation of model-supplied input against each tool's declared JSON Schema before dispatching to its executor.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` describing required, type and enum failures without invoking the executor; rejection text and logs name property paths and constraints without revealing input values, while accepted input including unknown keys passes through unchanged without coercion or defaults, exactly once, and unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects malformed tool input privately and passes accepted input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L21)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration, invalid schemas throw with the tool name at registration, and executing ten calls does not recompile the schema. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved for each execution and validated using the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name. ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema and reuses schema objects](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L104)).
+
+## Delivery notes
+
+Rejections are ordinary tool results available to the model for correction within the existing five-round conversation limit. Consumer documentation, a MINOR version bump, runtime validator dependency and migration changelog accompany implementation; executors that previously handled malformed input themselves will stop receiving it. Output validation, authorization, execution retries and changes to the unknown-tool exception are outside this issue.
